2026-07-23 cont550: *** ROOT-CAUSED the batched nan *** NOT a fused epilogue (bert bmms are pure matmul+fill). The real bug: spirv-cross BAKES the subspan BYTE-OFFSET into buffer indexing — original kernel reads _resource_var_0_0_._m0[786432 + ...] (786432 float4*16 = 12582912 B = binding(0) offset). IREE binds the WHOLE allocation at id0; the kernel adds the subspan offset. My substituted kernel reads from offset 0 -> wrong region -> nan. Attention bmm operands are subspans of a shared ~96MB alloc (offsets 12.5MB/96MB/12.5MB); the 2D FFN-bwd GEMMs happened to be offset-0 whole-buffer so validated correct — but this is a LATENT risk for the 2D path too (any offset-bound matmul would corrupt). FIX (both paths): extract per-binding base offset (from SPIR-V access chains / mslSource `+ <N>u` base) and add to the tensor_inline base pointer: device T* Ab = s.A + baseOff + b*M*K. Until then, correctness guard = fall back if any binding has a non-zero subspan offset. Batched path stays gated (IREE_METAL_MSL4_BMM off). Next: implement offset extraction OR the offset-0 guard in tryEmitMatmul2dMSL.
