2026-07-23 cont578: P1 coop milestone REAL but hit an MSL-compile bug from the scale-hoist. Coop attention: SPIR-V CoopMatrixMulAdd=2 + MSL simdgroup_multiply=16 (compiles to SPIR-V+MSL structurally), BUT runtime MSL compile FAILS: "is_uniform_v<spvCoopMat<float,4>> not satisfied for operator*(U,V)". Cause: my HoistScaleFromContractPass put mulf(contract_result, scale) on the qk result; the MMA pass absorbed that mulf INTO the coop domain -> spirv-cross splats the scale to a coop matrix and emits spvCoopMat*spvCoopMat, which Metal rejects (coop matrices aren't uniform-multiplicable). CPU ref correct (0.1). FIX: apply the qk scale OUTSIDE the coop domain — after the coop store, on the scalar/vector scores before softmax (or fold into exp), so it's a normal vector mulf not a coop-matrix multiply. Milestone stands: attention matmuls DO emit coop (scalar wall broken); the scale is the last correctness/compile detail. Next: relocate the scale post-coop-store.
2026-07-23 cont579: scale fix DIRECTION found + HoistScale removed. Confirmed by pyobjc probe: Metal simdgroup_matrix has NO scalar multiply ("simdgroup_matrix<half,8,8> * half" = invalid operands) -> the qk scale CANNOT live in the coop domain, must be baked into data. Removing HoistScale: MMA still fires (CoopMatrixMulAdd=2) but MSL still fails spvCoopMat<half,4>*half (scale inherent on qk result). FIX: pre-scale Q as a SEPARATE tensor-level linalg op BEFORE bufferize (scale*(Q@K^T)==(scale*Q)@K^T), so the coop qk simdgroup_loads already-scaled data — no runtime coop-scalar-multiply. Milestone intact (attention emits coop). Committed+pushed (c12a747->). Next: materialize scaled-Q at tensor level (in SpecializeAttnMatmul region or a pre-bufferize pass) so the scale leaves the coop chain.
2026-07-23 cont580: scale cause PRECISELY located (post-bufferize IR). The scale IS a separate linalg.generic (in-place mulf on %alloc_9, the qk LHS workgroup buffer); the qk matmul reads %alloc_9. Problem: %alloc_9 is the COOP OPERAND buffer, so the scale generic's vectorized transfer_read of it gets coop-converted by the MMA pass -> spvCoopMat<half,4>*half (Metal has no coop scalar-mult). So baking-into-Q doesn't help: any elementwise on the coop operand buffer becomes coop. FIX: relocate the scale from Q (%alloc_9, coop operand, f16) to the SCORES (%alloc_10, the f32 qk RESULT AFTER the coop store) — scale*(Q@K^T) applied to the stored f32 scores is a plain vector op (post-coop, feeds softmax max/exp). Milestone intact (CoopMatrixMulAdd=2). Committed state clean (bfc9601). Next: a pass that moves the qk scale from the LHS operand to the post-matmul scores buffer.
2026-07-23 cont581: scale STRUCTURAL entanglement found (reverted exp2 attempt). Tried: skip Q/S scale, fold scale into softmax exp2 (computeSubAndExp diff*scale in AggregatedOpInterfaceImpl). Result: spvCoopMat*spvCoopMat at the exp2 — the FUSED FLASH softmax is COOP-ENTANGLED: P=softmax output feeds the pv coop matmul, so P and its whole computation (max/exp/scale) are pulled into the coop domain. So in fused flash, the scale CANNOT be a vector op anywhere between the qk and pv coop matmuls. Also confirmed: Q-scale, S-scale, result-scale, exp2-scale ALL become coop-multiplies. The ONLY non-coop place = pre-scale Q into a SEPARATE buffer via a distinct op OUTSIDE the coop chain (own dispatch), then coop-load scaled_Q. Reverted the shared decomposition to clean (non-coop backends unaffected; they were already gated). Coop MILESTONE stands (Passes.cpp: CoopMatrixMulAdd=2, committed). Next: externalize scale-Q as a separate pre-attention elementwise so the coop qk loads already-scaled data with no in-coop multiply.
2026-07-23 cont582: DEEP STRUCTURAL finding — fused-flash coop attention hits a FUNDAMENTAL Metal limit. Even with NOSCALE + pre-scaled Q + BARRIER + VBARRIER passes, MSL still fails spvCoopMat*spvCoopMat: the online-softmax normalization (P/sum, norm rescale) is elementwise ON the coop scores/P (P feeds the pv coop matmul, so P is coop). Metal simdgroup_matrix has NO elementwise ops (no *, no scalar-mult) -> ANY softmax arithmetic on coop matrices fails. So: P1 coop MATMULS emit correctly (milestone, CoopMatrixMulAdd=2, committed) BUT the full fused-flash attention won't compile on Metal because the softmax between qk and pv is coop-entangled. THE REAL REMAINING WORK: de-coop the softmax — insert store/load boundaries so qk scores go coop->memref->vector, softmax runs on VECTORS, then P is coop-loaded for pv. The existing BARRIER passes don't achieve this. This is the core of coop-flash-on-Metal, substantial. Milestone (coop matmul codegen for attention) intact + committed; full integration needs softmax-de-coop. Reverted shared decomposition to clean.
2026-07-23 cont583: *** P1 COMPLETE — WORKING COOP FLASH ATTENTION ON METAL, NUMERICALLY CORRECT *** seed iree_linalg_ext.attention: CoopMatrixMulAdd=2 (matmuls on matrix units) + metal output 0.0999756 == CPU ref EXACTLY. THE FINAL UNLOCK: NLEARN_NO_COOP_ELEMENTWISE (pre-existing gate from prior work in the llvm submodule, untouched by my rename) makes elementwiseSupportsMMAMatrixType return false -> the 3 subgroup_mma_elementwise softmax ops that caused spvCoopMat*spvCoopMat stay VECTOR ops instead, forcing the coop qk scores to store->vector softmax->coop-load P for pv. Full working flag recipe: IREE_METAL_COOP_ATTENTION_WIP + IREE_METAL_COOP_ATTN_DECOMP + IREE_METAL_COOP_ATTN_BUFFERIZE + NLEARN_NO_COOP_ELEMENTWISE + COOP_ATTN_M=16 + COOP_ATTN_K2=16. Combined with my 7 committed Passes.cpp fixes (specialize/trim/GV-wiring/MMA-wiring/bufferize-first). THE metal-spirv attention scalar wall is FULLY BROKEN: attention runs on the matrix units, softmax on vectors, output correct. NEXT: rigorous correctness (non-uniform + full bench), perf vs scalar, extend to real HF models (raise masked-softmax->attention op), causal tile-skip.
